<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="git-addon-file-conflict-solving-workflow">
  <title>Resolve File Conflicts</title>
  
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>conflict resolution</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>merge conflicts</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>rebase conflicts</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>
    <p id="p_ijj_gpy_kpb">If you try to push changes and
      <?oxy_comment_start author="adrian_lapadat" timestamp="20260529T114704+0300" comment="what specific warning?"?>a
      warning<?oxy_comment_end?> states that your local repository is not up to date with the remote
      repository, follow these steps:<ol id="ol_jjj_gpy_kpb">
        <li id="li_kjj_gpy_kpb">Pull the changes from the repository using one of the <xref
            href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_pull"
              ><uicontrol>Pull</uicontrol> actions</xref>.</li>
        <li id="li_ljj_gpy_kpb"
          ><?oxy_comment_start author="adrian_lapadat" timestamp="20260529T131001+0300" comment="if local is out of date with remote, that does not necessarily imply a conflict of any kind between the two branches, is that correct? if it is, info about merge conflicts should be moved or removed here. "?>In
          the <?oxy_comment_end?><xref
            href="git-addon-unstaged-files-area.dita#git-addon-unstaged-files-area" format="dita"
              ><uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area</xref>, select each conflicted file and
          resolve the conflicts. You can open each conflicted file in the compare editor by
          double-clicking it or by using the <xref
            href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_open"
              ><uicontrol>Open</uicontrol></xref> contextual menu action. Then choose which changes
          to keep, discard the changes that you do not need, and save the document. The contextual
          menu of a resource also includes <xref
            href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_resolve_using_mine"
              ><uicontrol>Resolve using Mine</uicontrol></xref>, <xref
            href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_resolve_using_theirs"
              ><uicontrol>Resolve using Theirs</uicontrol></xref>, and <xref
            href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_mark_as_resolved"
              ><uicontrol>Mark as resolved</uicontrol></xref>.</li>
        <li id="li_mjj_gpy_kpb">If you use the compare editor, after you close it, the file is
          staged automatically and moved to the <xref
            href="git-addon-staged-files-area.dita#git-addon-staged-files-area" format="dita"
              ><uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol> area</xref>.</li>
      </ol></p>
    <p id="p_git_conflict_state_panel">When a conflict is in progress, the <uicontrol>Git
        Staging</uicontrol> view shows a state label (for example,
      <uicontrol>Merging...</uicontrol>) above the file list so you can see whether you are
      resolving a merge, rebase, cherry-pick, or revert. The same area also shows the actions that
      are available for the current operation, such as <uicontrol>Abort Merge</uicontrol>,
        <uicontrol>Restart Merge</uicontrol>, <uicontrol>Abort Rebase</uicontrol>,
        <uicontrol>Continue Rebase</uicontrol>, <uicontrol>Abort Cherry-pick</uicontrol>, or
        <uicontrol>Abort Revert</uicontrol>.</p>
    <p id="p_git_conflict_state_panel_merge">During a merge, the conflict panel remains visible even
      after all conflicts are resolved and staged, so you can still abort or restart the merge before
      committing.</p>
    <p>
      <fig id="fig_wpt_g1p_ljc">
        <title>Merge Conflict on <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol></title>
        <image href="../img/git-addon/staging/merge-conflict-staging.png" id="image_ilr_j1p_ljc"/>
      </fig>
    </p>
    <p id="p_njj_gpy_kpb">The next steps depend on which <xref
        href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_pull"><uicontrol>Pull</uicontrol></xref>
      option you used:<ul id="ul_ojj_gpy_kpb">
        <li id="li_pjj_gpy_kpb">
          <p id="p_qjj_gpy_kpb"><xref
              href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_pull_merge"><uicontrol>Pull
                (merge)</uicontrol></xref>:<ol id="ol_rjj_gpy_kpb">
              <li id="li_sjj_gpy_kpb">When all conflicts are resolved and no files remain in the
                  <xref href="git-addon-unstaged-files-area.dita#git-addon-unstaged-files-area"
                  format="dita"><uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area</xref>, commit the
                changes.</li>
              <li id="li_tjj_gpy_kpb">Enter a commit message and commit. You now have new changes
                to push.</li>
              <li id="li_ujj_gpy_kpb">Push the changes to the remote repository.</li>
            </ol><note id="note_ymz_spy_kpb">You can abort the merge by clicking
                <xref
                  href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_abort_merge"><uicontrol>Abort
                    merge</uicontrol></xref>.</note></p>
        </li>
        <li id="li_wjj_gpy_kpb">
          <p id="p_xjj_gpy_kpb"><xref
              href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_pull_rebase"><uicontrol>Pull
                (rebase)</uicontrol></xref>:<ol id="ol_yjj_gpy_kpb">
              <li id="li_zjj_gpy_kpb">When all conflicts are resolved, click
                  <xref
                  href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_continue_rebase"><uicontrol>Continue
                    rebase</uicontrol></xref>.</li>
              <li id="li_akj_gpy_kpb">Push any outgoing changes.</li>
            </ol><note id="note_yh2_dqy_kpb">You can abort the rebase by clicking
                <xref
                  href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_abort_rebase"><uicontrol>Abort
                    rebase</uicontrol></xref>.</note></p>
        </li>
      </ul></p>
  </body>
</topic>